& [SJS]
  + Situation: Slice4B2A returns exact signed source identities line locators and span digests but not the admitted path or quoted bytes needed for direct inspection
  + Justification: resolving from the already admitted in-memory package is deterministic safer than rereading mutable files and small enough to test without semantic ranking or model behavior
  + Solution: add a separately replayed source-projection result and an optional laboratory flag that preserves no-flag output exactly

& [Delineation]
  + source projection proves correspondence to the admitted package snapshot only
  + source projection does not claim the live workspace is unchanged and does not infer truth purpose permission authority or action fitness
  + selecting a lexical match and quoting its source are separate stages with separate proof digests
  + a signed package path is descriptive metadata and never becomes an ambient filesystem capability

& [ReuseDecision]
  + SemanticFabric already retains admitted packages SourceSnapshot QuoteRecord SourceAnchor certificate identity and package digest
  + existing query projection demonstrates the exact package quote source correspondence but is private and coupled to CantorQueryRequest semantics
  + Slice4B2B therefore adds a dependency-light projection operator beside the catalogue lookup rather than widening the direct query protocol
  + projection uses admitted bytes only and does not duplicate trust admission

& [FormAndBudgetDecision]
  + each projection binds address anchor path text document digest certificate id and a domain-separated projection digest
  + the result binds profile lexical proof ordered projections fixed snapshot-boundary statement and result proof digest
  + maximum projections cannot exceed the lexical match hard cap
  + quote and serialized-result bytes are independently positive and hard capped
  + clipping is forbidden because disappearing matches would misrepresent proof completeness

& [TestDecision]
  + positive multiline path line text certificate and deterministic replay cases
  + stale lexical result missing package quote or source anchor conflicting package and invalid UTF-8 refusal cases where constructible
  + self-resealed path text document certificate anchor order omission addition and proof mutations
  + CLI no-flag compatibility include-source success repeatability and finite-budget refusal over tracked signed corpus

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty names the snapshot boundary and retains exact quoted bytes without summarization
  + Security forbids ambient path reads requires admitted package identity and refuses incomplete projection
  + Weaver connects lexical address to source anchor quote snapshot and certificate by exact identity only
  + Planner orders lexical replay package resolution source proof bounds digest and whole replay
  + Refiner adds one optional stage and no new ranking semantics
  + Scribe exposes human-readable path lines and text beside machine digests
  + Observer requires no-flag byte stability focused release workspace lint format evidence and diff gates

& [Disposition]
  + [Slice4B2B] ready_for_exact_phase_lock
  + [still_locked] semantic_query_composition_live_filesystem_and_all_provider_effect_remote_and_compiler_backend_behavior
